Fixed. The bug was in advanceTurn at src/sim.ts:43 — the growth check used `foodSurplus >= 0`, so a break-even turn (production exactly equal to consumption) still counted as a surplus and the population grew by 1 every turn, compounding until food went into deficit. Changed it to `foodSurplus > 0` so growth only happens on a real surplus.

I also added a regression test block for advanceTurn in tests/sim.test.ts covering all three cases (surplus grows, break-even holds, deficit holds) — the old suite never touched advanceTurn, which is why the bug slipped through.

Verification: npm run test — 7/7 passing, npm run typecheck — clean.


